-- A WITH that names a binder the callee reads under two same-spelled binders,
-- and is neither of them: there is no way to tell which was meant.
--
-- The remedy is R3's other two: rename one of them, or hoist them to a common
-- section heading if they are one thing.

§ `1`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
h1 MEANS foo TIMES 1

§ `2`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
h2 MEANS foo TIMES 100

§ `3`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
g MEANS h1 PLUS h2

GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS g WITH foo IS foo
